--TEST--
`Core\Reflect\ClassInfo::get` is the ordinary erased read: a `get` hook runs once per read, and a `lateinit` property never written throws — `rule:security/reflection-enforces-visibility`, `rule:classes/property-hooks`, `rule:classes/an-unwritten-property-read-throws`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Reflect\ClassInfo::get
// A reflective read answers what `$value->name` on a `mixed` answers. Reading
// the slot directly would give the hook's empty backing store, which is not
// an `int`, and an unwritten slot's storage state instead of a throw.
class Counter {
    public int $hits = 0;

    public int $value {
        get {
            $this->hits = $this->hits + 1;
            return 10;
        }
    }

    public function constructor() {
    }
}

var $counter = new Counter();
var $described = Core\Reflect::forObject($counter);
echo $counter->value, "\n";
echo $described->get($counter, "value") as int, "\n";
// Two reads, two runs of the hook.
echo $counter->hits, "\n";

class Ring {
    public lateinit Ring $next;
    public function constructor(public string $name) {}
}

var $ring = new Ring("a");
var $ringInfo = Core\Reflect::forObject($ring);
try {
    var $next = $ringInfo->get($ring, "next");
    echo "unwritten read", "\n";
} catch (RuntimeError $unwritten) {
    echo $unwritten->message, "\n";
}
// Once written, the same read answers the value.
$ring->next = new Ring("b");
echo ($ringInfo->get($ring, "next") as Ring)->name, "\n";
--EXPECT--
10
10
2
`Ring`'s property `$next` is read before it is written
b
